     1	# Where the EE actually lives — the layer map, after today's deflations
     2	
     3	**2026-09-10 10:20 UTC.** Every figure carries reference / information class / estimand /
     4	numerator. A figure that cannot carry all four is not listed.
     5	
     6	## The map
     7	
     8	| layer | size | reference | information | numerator | owned by a learned route? |
     9	|---|---:|---|---|---|---|
    10	| carrier incumbent -> one-shot per-user best response | **`~+400%`** | carrier incumbent | nominal, exact surplus | pooled EE | **No.** Head-independent argmax |
    11	| one-shot -> converged unilateral fixed point | remainder to `+664%` (`SEALED`) / `+451%` (`MARGIN_Q`) | carrier incumbent | nominal | pooled EE | **No.** 45-65 s of search |
    12	| fixed point -> bounded joint optimum | **`+0.899%`** (8 anchors) / **`+1.29%`** (20 anchors) | **correctly-paired unilateral fixed point** | nominal, strict clearance | pooled **demand-capped** | **C3's natural home** |
    13	| fixed assignment, control law (power/mode) | **`+1.93%`** under corrected `STRICT`; `+82.78%` under defective `SEALED` | declared control law | **non-causal, best-known search** | demand-capped | **No route** |
    14	| route 2 (persistence) | **no EE measurement of any kind** | — | — | — | C2, and v1.9 §5 declares its set-level marginal zero by construction |
    15	
    16	## What changed today in this map
    17	
    18	**The control-law pillar deflated.** It was quoted at `+119%` / `+134%` on the capacity
    19	numerator. Under the demand cap it is **`+1.93%`** on the corrected `STRICT` rule. The
    20	`+82.78%` figure belongs to `SEALED`, the **defective** provisioning rule under which
    21	**0 of 800** user-anchors attain the target, so the cap binds nothing. That number describes
    22	a broken regime, not available headroom.
    23	
    24	`SWEEP-fable` predicted this before `CTRLCAP` reported: *"STRICT demand-capped gain in the
    25	low single digits or less; SEALED larger because 0/800 attained."* Both halves correct. That
    26	audit predicted an unrun measurement, which is the strongest evidence of its reliability
    27	available.
    28	
    29	## The consequence for the claim
    30	
    31	Two of the three large numbers that appeared to sit outside the learned routes are now gone:
    32	the multi-start `9.87%` was an order statistic under the defective rule, and the control law
    33	is `+1.93%` once corrected and capped. **The one large thing that remains is the per-user
    34	best-response step**, and it is reached by a plain exact-surplus argmax with no head at all.
    35	
    36	So the question the three routes must answer is **not** "does this system have headroom". It
    37	is: **after the head-independent best-response step, is there room that belongs to learning?**
    38	
    39	The only measurement of that question in existence is
    40	`FULL - ALL_NEUTRAL_CONTROL = -0.01745324091886997`
    41	*ref: `ALL_NEUTRAL_CONTROL` · info: as-run panel smoke · estimand: relative pooled-EE marginal
    42	· numerator: pooled EE* — identical under both provisioning rules, and **negative**. It was
    43	measured on the surrogate corpus with the defective 12-effective-dimension feature schema, so
    44	it is not final; but it is the only reading of the actual question that exists.
    45	
    46	## What is running to change that
    47	
    48	| job | question | why it can settle something alone |
    49	|---|---|---|
    50	| `SCHEMA2` | a repaired Q1 schema: elevation added, dead slots repaired, effective dimension recorded | `C1REAL`'s "informational ceiling" verdict is confounded with the defect |
    51	| `C2REAL` | is the declared C2 target learnable at all | if not, route 2 is finished as declared, with no corpus, no panel, no EE run |
    52	| `C3REAL` (queued) | same, for the residual head | same |
    53	| `EXACTGEN2` | exact-path corpus, physics serialised separately from the feature view | needed under every branch, and the separation stops a feature change forcing a regeneration |
    54	| `OBJMISMATCH` | are the certified endpoints locally optimal under the reported objective | independent half of the residual-sign question |
    55	
    56	**None of these needs `D1` decided first**, and none needs the others.
