FILE controller-records/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v0-2026-09-08.md
     1	# V025 stages 6–8 contract v0 — source generation, learner, evaluation (controller draft for sealing; 2026-09-08 ≈ 18:10 UTC; no successor training exists)
     2	
     3	Pipeline audit B/C/D verified that the successor has no implemented path from tapes to a trained, deployed, evaluated policy: stages 6–8 exist as prose. This contract fixes the declarations so that implementation can start now in parallel with the physics matrix; nothing in it is conditioned on a matrix or training outcome, and the matrix admission decision (PHYSICS-GO) remains the only trigger for real training.
     4	
     5	## Stage 6 — source rows
     6	1. **Producer:** tapes (provider decisions 9–11) → per (anchor, user, legal action) rows built by one production builder; every row carries world/user/action/time/calibration lineage; TRAIN-only asserted at construction.
     7	2. **Q1 schema (successor, replaces the legacy 228-D):** per action: nominal current fields (SINR margin at rate target, required power / cap, mode SE, occupancy excluding focal, beam-active and satellite-active bits before focal insertion, off-axis angle, D2 remaining time, visibility remaining time, refresh phase), plus the migrated historical tail (previous served association one-hot, previous served load per candidate, previous beam/satellite activity, previous beam max RF / cap), plus `missing_incumbent`; **no** recurrence power, entry-gain ratio or segment age. Exact field list, scales and schema SHA are sealed in v1 of this contract.
     8	3. **Q2 schema:** the frozen 21-field C2 schema completed with `missing_incumbent` and the declared background semantics: background = previous committed served set excluding the focal user, timestamp = decision instant, occupancy excludes focal, activation measured before focal insertion.
     9	4. **Labels:** C1 whole-network surplus + Φ (bits / κ); C2 three-offset forecast core with −κ per absorbing lost offset (bits / κ); C3 interaction share only (Ψ/2 pairs; Shapley for sets) over the sealed bounded catalogue; κ per stage-4 item 24; all prices explicit.
    10	5. **Dependency allowlist:** every label is a function of the visible primitives, masks, keyed fading and declared state only (stage-4 item 25); a golden tape-to-row fixture asserts every field.
    11	
    12	## Stage 7 — learner and deployment
    13	6. **Learner contract:** pairwise zero-bootstrap regression on typed deterministic aggregate batches (the legacy heterogeneous Catfish design), one versioned schema; no Bellman replay in the successor. Epoch = one deterministic pass over the sealed batches (row counts, order and digests sealed); checkpoints every 100 source epochs with `completed_source_epochs`, route-update count and batch digests; resume authenticated.
    14	7. **Arms:** FULL, DROP_C1, DROP_C2, DROP_C3 by **neutral-source substitution** for the named route (all heads retained and deployed, as in the legacy orchestrator), ALL_NEUTRAL_CONTROL (all routes neutral), external BASELINE; the estimand is "informative vs neutral source training for that route".
    15	8. **Seeds and CRN:** five learner seeds (v1.0 evaluation design governs over the round-3 "three initializations"), each lineage sharing one serialised initialisation and identical source batches across arms; `learner_seed` and `world_seed` are separate fields everywhere.
    16	9. **Deployed selector:** per-user masked argmax of the normalised Q1 + Q2 sum (bits / κ) for the two-head policy; the C3 layer is the set-level coordinator (learned S3 or exact S0) over the bounded catalogue with the sealed service guard, a 30.08 s deadline, BASE-proposal fallback, and the deployment-capability manifest (stage-4 item 26); the information-matched `S_UNI` comparator is always evaluated beside it.
    17	10. **Joint feasibility:** the committed action is one jointly legal profile; independent per-user argmax outputs are validated as a profile before commit (KAT: two users whose individually legal picks are jointly infeasible).
    18	
    19	## Stage 8 — evaluation and claim
    20	11. **Panel:** the sealed design (6 arms × 5 learner seeds × ≈ 600 TRAIN worlds over ≈ 161 dates; ≈ 30 steps per world) with a prospective allocation manifest (decision CD-6); cluster = TLE date × learner seed; no TEST split.
    21	12. **Endpoint and statistics:** pooled ΣB/ΣE with the cluster bootstrap recomputing the ratio per draw; δ = +0.5 pp lower-bound rule per FULL − DROP contrast; QoS margins per stage-2 decision 6; supplementary delta-method and two-way intervals; conditional intersection–union claim wording (v1.2 §4); multiplicity: the claim is the conjunction, no per-contrast inflation.
    22	13. **Harness discipline:** attempt registry (CD-2), canonical per-step receipts (CD-5), conformance suite (CD-7), same physics/endpoint code digest as training, one terminal adjudication.
    23	14. **Order of operations:** implementation and synthetic end-to-end tests now; source generation only after the calibration freeze and the matrix admission (PHYSICS-GO); training in the pipeline session; early rungs integrity-only; checkpoints every 100 source epochs; the owner is notified before any long continuation.

FILE controller-records/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md
     1	# V025 stages 6–8 contract v1 — source generation, learner, evaluation (controller; sealed 2026-09-08 ≈ 18:45 UTC; supersedes v0; no successor training exists)
     2	
     3	Sources folded in: astra contract review (`ADJUDICATION-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-CODEX-GPT6-ASTRA-2026-09-08.md`), round-7 outside opinions (Q&A + Deep Research), pipeline audits B/C/D, first-principles review. All three reviewers returned `CONTRACT=REVISE`, `C3_IDENTIFIABLE=NO` as written, `POWERED=NO`; v1 resolves each named item. Nothing here is conditioned on any outcome.
     4	
     5	## A. Information interfaces (declared, equalised across arms)
     6	A1. **I_heads** (per user i, per legal action): the completed Q1 and Q2 schemas of §B; observation access = current nominal geometry of user i's candidates, i's history, the previous committed served set excluding i (b⁻₋ᵢ) at decision time; derived features as frozen; model access = none (no joint physics); compute = one forward pass.
     7	A2. **I_coordinator** (per anchor): global nominal geometry with beam-specific cross gains, all users' legal sets, b⁻, the reference proposal a⁰, the bounded catalogue 𝒞 (decision 4/CB-2), the nominal model 𝓜 (no realised fading, no future TLE beyond the declared forecast horizon), and the outputs of 𝓜 for each profile in 𝒞 (joint load, coupled powers, interference, activation, service, bits, energy, continuation). Compute = the declared budget (§F).
     8	A3. **Two distinct references:** a⁰ (the reference proposal for the score decomposition; = the per-user argmax of Q1 + Q2, validated as a profile) and the previous committed association (the reference for handover/Φ/event accounting). Never conflated.
     9	A4. **Equalised between FULL and every DROP/comparator arm:** primitive access and timestamps, forecast method, physical identities, catalogue construction (authenticated identical catalogues at matched anchors), joint search, guards, tie-breaking, validation, deadline, fallback. Any learned pruning is part of the declared intervention. An exact evaluator may never reinsert a removed score through ranking, pruning or a score-dependent guard.
    10	
    11	## B. Stage 6 — rows and labels
    12	B1. One production builder from tapes; every row carries world/user/action/time/schema/setting/calibration lineage; TRAIN asserted at construction; dependency-allowlist KAT (labels are functions of visible primitives, masks, keyed fading, declared state only).
    13	B2. **Q1 schema** (per action; scales frozen in the spec v1 draft): nominal rate-target SINR margin, required power / cap, mode SE, occupancy excluding focal, beam- and satellite-active bits before focal insertion, off-axis angle, remaining D2 time, remaining visibility time, refresh phase; history: previous served association one-hot, previous served load per candidate, previous beam/satellite activity, previous beam max RF / cap; `missing_incumbent`. No recurrence power, entry-gain ratio or segment age.
    14	B3. **Q2 schema:** the frozen 21 fields + `missing_incumbent`; background = b⁻₋ᵢ projected to the decision instant; occupancy excludes focal; activation before focal insertion.
    15	B4. **F and Φ:** F(a) = B(a) − η_ref·E(a) − Φ(a), with Φ the signed handover/QoS preference in κ units charged exactly once inside F. Unilateral increments dᵢ = F(aᵢ, a⁰₋ᵢ) − F(a⁰); interaction residual Ψ_A = F(a_A, a⁰₋A) − F(a⁰) − Σᵢ∈A dᵢ. **C1(config) = Σᵢ∈A dᵢ; C3(config) = Ψ_A; identity C1 + C3 = F(a_A) − F(a⁰) exactly** (KAT); a second KAT states the physical identity without Φ. C2 = declared continuation value excluding the immediate term (three offsets, −κ per absorbing lost offset). κ per stage-4 item 24; all in bits / κ.
    16	B5. **C3 training rows** carry the complete coalition context: anchor, a⁰, the changed-user set A, their selected actions a_A, the global resource context (occupancy, activation, shared capacity, interference summary per affected beam), and the label Ψ_A / κ. Coalition size for label computation is capped at |A| ≤ 4 (2^|A| subset evaluations bounded); larger evacuation sets are labelled by the capped decomposition and flagged. Per-user Shapley credit is reporting only (pairs: Ψ/2 each), never a training target.
    17	
    18	## C. Stage 7 — learner, arms, deployment
    19	C1. **Heads:** Q1, Q2 by pairwise zero-bootstrap regression on typed deterministic aggregate batches (legacy heterogeneous design); the deployed two-head action is the per-user masked argmax of the normalised Q1 + Q2, validated as a jointly legal profile (deterministic repair rule for conflicts, KAT with a jointly infeasible pair). This estimates a supervised surrogate of the declared targets, not a Bellman value; the claim is worded accordingly.
    20	C2. **C3 learner form:** a **set-conditioned scalar interaction head** Ψ̂_θ(Z_t, a⁰, A, a_A): permutation-invariant over A, anchored Ψ̂(∅) = Ψ̂({u}) = 0, trained on the residual Ψ_A / κ over the coalition support of the bounded catalogue; deployed S3 optimises the **complete** score C1 + C2 + Ψ̂ over 𝒞 with the sealed service guard, budget and fallback. S0 = the same selector with the exact Ψ_A in place of Ψ̂. S_UNI = iterated exact unilateral improvement to a local optimum (every legal unilateral alternative evaluated with the same nominal joint physics at each iterate, deterministic improving move, atomic commit of the final profile only, termination certificate reported).
    21	C3. **Arms and estimands (four named experiments, never conflated):** (i) *learned neutral-source experiment* (primary for the C1/C2/C3 claims): FULL, DROP_C1, DROP_C2, DROP_C3 by neutral-source substitution of the named route with all routes retained, updated and deployed; ALL_NEUTRAL_CONTROL; external BASELINE; claim wording: "informative source training for route x improved pooled EE relative to the specified neutral source training, with the other routes informative and all heads retained"; (ii) *oracle factor-score removal* (physics regime map, stage-4 item 18); (iii) *checkpoint knockout* (secondary: zero the deployed contribution, machinery fixed; measures reliance and exposes hidden score restoration); (iv) *architecture removal* — named, not run.
    22	C4. **Coordination attribution (beyond the source claim):** FULL (S3) > DROP_C3 **and** FULL > the S_UNI-equipped comparator on held-out realised pooled EE, QoS margins met, plus decision-relevant nonadditivity (the selected profile differs from the additive/unilateral optimum at a reported fraction of anchors, including rejected harmful joint moves) — the requirement "g_I ≠ 0" is withdrawn. **Learned value (S3 vs matched S0)** is one predeclared axis: realised closed-loop pooled EE under equal computation budget including timeouts; matching S0 at lower compute is an acceleration claim, reported separately.
    23	C5. **Neutral sources** sealed before generation: generator, labels, support, strata, overlap, row weights, optimisation dose; "identical batches across arms" means identical within a route/source identity; every DROP checkpoint retains all heads, the neutral-trained head differs from initialisation and participates in deployment (KATs).
    24	C6. **Zero results are allowed and informative:** a zero C3 source marginal ends the positive C3 claim under this scope; an interval excluding the practical margin supports "no practically relevant benefit"; a lower-bound failure alone is inconclusive; neither permits changing features, catalogues, sources or regimes until C3 becomes positive.
    25	C7. **Epochs, checkpoints, seeds:** deterministic aggregate epochs with sealed row counts/order/digests; checkpoints every 100 source epochs with `completed_source_epochs` and batch digests; **12 learner seeds** (§E), each lineage sharing one serialised initialisation and identical source batches per route identity across arms; `learner_seed` and `world_seed` separate everywhere.
    26	
    27	## D. Stage 8 — panel, statistics, harness
    28	D1. **Panel:** 6 arms × 12 learner seeds × 2 worlds per TRAIN date over the ≈ 160 claim dates (≈ 320 worlds per arm-seed; ≈ 30 steps per world), allocation manifest sealed with role-wise date disjointness (claim dates unused by any successor development activity; legacy overlap recorded); no TEST.
    29	D2. **Estimator:** pooled ΣB/ΣE; primary interval = two-way pigeonhole bootstrap over dates × learner seeds with arms paired within resamples and the ratio recomputed per draw (central 95 % percentile); one-way cluster bootstrap and delta-method supplementary; seedwise paired effects reported; δ = +0.5 % relative with the 2.5th-percentile lower bound (v1.4); QoS margins with additive numerators/denominators inside draws (stage-2 decision 6, item 37).
    30	D3. **Zero outcomes:** B = 0 with E > 0 is EE = 0 (defined); a draw is undefined only when a denominator (E or the comparator's EE) is 0 — recorded and counted, never substituted (amends decision CD-3).
    31	D4. **Multiplicity and claim:** the conditional intersection–union conjunction for `a-r0` is the single primary claim; components are reported with their own intervals but no component-wise discovery is claimed; all other cells exploratory; TRAIN-only wording enforced by the report schema.
    32	D5. **Harness:** attempt registry (STARTED before outcomes), canonical per-step receipts, merge re-aggregation from rows, conformance suite (NULL ≡ BASE per step, real-step dry-run of every arm, write-once sha256 receipts, authority manifest), same physics/endpoint digest as training, one terminal adjudication.
    33	
    34	## E. Power (declared prospectively; sensitivities, not measurements)
    35	Planning alternative Δ* = +2 % relative (both reviewers: a true +1 % is not detectable with ≈ 160 dates under any seed count if the date SD is ≈ 5 %). Variance sensitivities: date SD 3 / 5 / 10 %, seed SD 1 / 2 %. With date SD 5 %, seed SD 1 %, 160 dates, 12 seeds and negligible residual variance, the per-contrast one-sided power at the 2.5 % level is ≈ 0.86 (SE ≈ 0.49 %); the three-contrast conjunction ≈ 0.64 if independent. With 5 seeds it is ≈ 0.70 / 0.34. 12 seeds is the declared design; the date component caps further gains. The crossed-cluster inference test (§G T3) calibrates the actual procedure at 5 and 12 seeds before any real evaluation.
    36	
    37	## F. Operational contract (deployability; the benchmark and the operational claim are separate)
    38	F1. **Benchmark convention:** decision at t from information at t, applied from t (legacy convention, kept for the scientific comparison); TLE nearest-epoch rule labelled retrospective (v1.5 §5). **Operational claim** (if made): a causal-input variant (ephemeris available by decision time, causal forecasts) and an explicit action-effective-time convention.
    39	F2. **Timing budget:** the coordinator's compute budget is 10 s wall on the declared worker count (the rest of the 30.08 s interval reserved for sensing/transport/validation/commit); BASE (a⁰) is computed, validated and repaired **before** the coordinator starts; the runner enforces the timer (cancel), not the solver; a miss executes the validated a⁰; misses are a co-reported QoS field and their B/E enter the endpoint.
    40	F3. **Capability manifest fields:** telemetry sources and ages, roster and cross-gain coverage, model assumptions and calibration source, worker hardware/count, catalogue bounds, solver limits, memory, missing-data handling, measured end-to-end latency distribution.
    41	
    42	## G. Synthetic acceptance tests — mandatory gate before any real source generation
    43	T1 **Exhaustive decomposition and intervention:** hand-computed 3-user, 2-action, 3-step fixture with additive / synergistic (F = 0, −1, −1, 2) / antagonistic (0, −1, −1, −4) cases, a dummy user (credit 0), nonzero Φ charged once, a future outage; production target builder and selectors; exact reconstruction of both identities; oracle DROP behaviour as hand-predicted; neutral-source DROP retains and trains the route; knockout removes the deployed contribution.
    44	T2 **Information twins / interaction reversal / additive placebo through the production path:** paired contexts with identical per-user rows but opposite joint interactions; S3 must separate them using declared coalition context and fail when it is removed; poisoned post-decision outcomes, realised future fading and hidden legacy reset state leave current features and actions unchanged; physical-identity relabelling invariance; jointly infeasible individual proposals repaired; an injected timeout exercises the real fallback; the additive placebo yields Ψ̂ ≈ 0 and S3 = S_UNI decisions.
    45	T3 **Crossed-cluster inference through the real merger:** synthetic raw receipts with controlled date/seed/world effects for the 3/5/10 % SD scenarios, repeated worlds per cell, unequal energies (pooled ≠ mean EE), identical arms, zero-bit and undefined-denominator cells, injected alternatives, least-favourable conjunction null (one component at the +0.5 % boundary); verify pairing, interval calibration, conjunction power and QoS rejection at 5 and 12 seeds.
    46	
    47	## H. Order of operations
    48	Build 1 (running) → build 2 applies this v1 and implements T1–T3 → fresh-context audit of the build → controller seal of spec v1 → real source generation only after the calibration freeze **and** PHYSICS-GO (a-r0 admission); training in the pipeline session with checkpoints every 100 source epochs; the owner is notified before any long continuation.
    49	
    50	Seal: sha256 in the companion `.sha256` file. v0 is retained as history.

