    11	level `R²` was `−0.2724` (bootstrap interval `[−0.5750, −0.0435]`) and top-1 accuracy was
    12	`0.1711`, indistinguishable in practical terms from the constant floor `0.1716`.
    13	
    14	[INFERRED] Widening does not rescue the head. A flexible nonlinear function of the same
    15	16 slots raises LOAO `R²` to only `0.0933`, ordering to `0.6197`, and top-1 to `0.1854`,
    16	then loses level transfer under leave-one-world-out (LOWO: `R² = −0.0714`). Therefore the
    17	dominant observed ceiling looks informational. There is also an architectural/optimization
    18	penalty—the flexible fit is better than the sealed head in level `R²`—but it is not the
    19	load-bearing explanation because widths 32 and 128 do not improve reliably and the best
