     7	## Verified by running code
     8	
     9	### Parity gate and invariant
    10	
    11	C1 replay passed the controller-declared 2-ULP gate: 54 of 54 floating fields were exact, 0 differed by 1 ULP, 0 by 2 ULP, and 0 exceeded 2 ULP (maximum 0 ULP). All 36 C1 count fields matched exactly.
    12	
    13	As a schedule-identity cross-check, C2 replay had 46 of 54 floating fields exact, 4 at 1 ULP, 4 at 2 ULP, and 0 above 2 ULP (maximum 2 ULP); all 36 C2 counts matched.
    14	
    15	The literal binary64 integrated-delivery invariant does **not** hold for all 1600 user-anchors: 2 violations were found. The minimum observed `C2 − C1` delivery was -2.384185791015625e-07 bit. Every violation is listed below.
    16	
    17	| Rule | Anchor | User | C1 served | C1 delivery (bit) | C2 delivery (bit) | C2 − C1 (bit) |
